it between Solid/Safe R and Likely R", "DCCC added the district to its target list and Barringer raised over $1.1M", "No public general-election polling in the race"], "rationale": "The district's R+8 lean, Knott's incumbency, and a rating consensus around Solid-to-Likely R point to a clear Republican edge, and markets price the Democrat near 18%. Democratic interest is real — Barringer's fundraising and the DCCC's targeting justify a modest Democratic nudge — but nothing suggests the seat is at true tossup risk.", "watch": "A late wave of Democratic outside spending or polling showing Knott under 50% against a well-funded challenger would signal a tighter race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Brad Knott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "NC-13 is a Republican-leaning open-map district where first-term incumbent Brad Knott is running for reelection against Democrat Paul Barringer and a Libertarian nominee. The seat's fundamentals favor the GOP by about eight points, and most expert raters place it in the Solid or Likely Republican column, though several outlets list it as only Likely R. Barringer has run a serious campaign, raising roughly $1.1 million, and national Democrats have added the district to their target list, citing concerns about Trump's standing in some of North Carolina's reddest seats. Still, no public general-election polling exists, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-five chance. The forecast expects Knott to win by a mid-to-high single-digit margin, with meaningful but limited uncertainty given the absence of polls.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0835, "margin": -8.64}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1064, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1381, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0942, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026